{"auditVerdictAtHead":"pass","canonicalDigest":"sha256:233aa7623c18198abd8b2254f1fa398595833a92c68afceefca25d89aeb5124f","canonicalizationVersion":"1","changeRequest":{"author":"buger","body":"Fixes #14150.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> Remove > Theme now shows only when there is a theme to remove, like the other Remove rows. Before, on a machine with no hand-installed themes (most of them), the row ran `omarchy-theme-remove`, which found nothing, printed \"No extra themes installed.\" where nobody could see it, and the menu just closed.\n\n| `~/.config/omarchy/themes` holds | `quattro` `a85e29a` | This PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| nothing (stock install), or the folder is missing | Theme row shown; Enter only closes the menu | no Theme row |\n| a theme copied or cloned there | Theme row; Enter opens the \"Remove extra theme\" picker | unchanged |\n| only a symlinked theme (a working copy, which the script never lists) | Theme row; Enter only closes the menu | no Theme row |\n| only a dot-directory such as `.git` (which the script lists but refuses to remove) | Theme row; the picker offers `.git`, and picking it does nothing | no Theme row; and next to a real theme the picker no longer offers `.git` |\n\n### What changes\n\n`remove.theme` gets `\"when\":\"omarchy-theme-removable\"`, a new helper that lists the themes `omarchy-theme-remove` can remove (directories under `~/.config/omarchy/themes` that are not symlinks or dot-directories) and exits nonzero when there are none. The remover now reads its list from the same helper, so the row and the picker can't disagree.\n\n```diff\n-  \"remove.theme\": {\"icon\":\"󰸌\",\"label\":\"Theme\",\"action\":\"omarchy-theme-remove\"},\n+  \"remove.theme\": {\"icon\":\"󰸌\",\"label\":\"Theme\",\"when\":\"omarchy-theme-removable\",\"action\":\"omarchy-theme-remove\"},\n```\n\nThis is the shape #7775 settled on for Update > Extra Themes (`omarchy-theme-extras`), and it is how the menu docs say Remove rows work: \"hiding via `when:` what is not there to remove\".\n\n<details><summary>Notes</summary>\n\n- `omarchy-theme-removable` is a plain bash glob, `~/.config/omarchy/themes/*`. That skips dot-directories, and being its own script keeps it out of reach of options a login shell set for the guard batch, which is #7775's reason too. A themes folder that is itself a symlink offers nothing, as the old `find` did.\n- Guards re-run every time the menu opens. The menu first draws with the previous answers and updates when the batch lands, about half a second later, as for every guarded row. So installing or removing a theme shows or hides the row on the next open. I checked this in a running shell.\n- `omarchy theme remove <name>` from a terminal is unchanged and still prints its message there.\n\n</details>\n\nA 76-second narrated capture of the real shell under Quickshell, with keys from a virtual keyboard. On upstream `quattro` `a85e29a`, Remove > Theme only closes the menu. On this branch's head `9a160c1` the row is hidden, and it comes back, opening the picker, once a theme is installed by hand:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2fc874c8-b573-4ba9-b72d-ff2070c4fc85\n\n### How to check it\n\n- [x] `test/shell.d/menu-test.sh` pins `remove.theme`'s `when:` to `omarchy-theme-removable`, as it pins `update.themes`.\n- [x] `test/shell.d/menu-guards-test.sh`, new block: the shipped `remove.theme` row goes through the guard script `MenuModel.guardScript` generates for it, against twelve homes: folder missing, empty, a copied theme, a cloned theme, only a symlinked theme, a theme with a `.git` file, only a `.git` directory, only a `.backup` directory, a `.git` directory next to a real theme, only a stray file, a theme named `-n`, and a themes folder that is a symlink into dotfiles. For each, it checks that the guard agrees with whether `omarchy-theme-remove` opened its picker and offered it a theme it would remove. It also checks that next to a real theme the picker is offered that theme and not `.git`. A stub picker returns nothing, so nothing is ever removed.\n- [x] it fails on `quattro`'s menu (`missing: guard=0 expected=1`) and with `quattro`'s remover (the picker is offered `.git`). Every mutation of the helper I tried makes it fail: counting symlinks, files or dot-directories, always or never succeeding, printing paths instead of names, printing with `echo` (a theme named `-n` disappears), following a symlinked themes folder, no filter at all.\n- [x] the menu suites still pass: `menu-test` 128 (127 + the new pin), `menu-guards` 21 (18 + 3 new), `menu-plugin` 12, `menu-images` 6, `keybindings-menu` 16, `app-search` 24, `theme-install-guards` 12\n- [x] the full `./test/shell` run fails the same 18 of 294 files before and after (my Linux box isn't an Omarchy install). None of them is a menu or theme test.\n- [x] in the real shell (summons over IPC, keys from `wtype`): on `quattro` with an empty themes folder, Enter on Theme closes the menu and no picker starts. On this branch the row is absent. After `mkdir ~/.config/omarchy/themes/my-theme` the row appears on the next open and Enter opens \"Remove extra theme\" listing `my-theme`. With only a symlinked theme, or only a `.git` directory, it is hidden again. With `.git` next to `my-theme`, `quattro`'s picker lists `.git` and `my-theme`; this branch's lists `my-theme`.\n\n<details><summary>Commands</summary>\n\n```sh\nbash test/shell.d/menu-test.sh\nbash test/shell.d/menu-guards-test.sh\n\n# the same tests against quattro's menu (expect: not ok - Remove > Theme shows exactly when omarchy-theme-remove has a theme to offer)\ngit checkout a85e29a -- default/omarchy/omarchy-menu.jsonc && bash test/shell.d/menu-guards-test.sh; git checkout HEAD -- default/omarchy/omarchy-menu.jsonc\n```\n\n</details>\n\n### What it could affect\n\nWhether the Remove > Theme row is listed, and the picker no longer listing dot-directories, which it refused to remove anyway. When `~/.config/omarchy/themes` is itself a symlink into someone's dotfiles, the picker offers nothing there, as before (the old `find` didn't descend into it either), and the row now stays hidden. `omarchy theme remove <name>` from a terminal is unchanged.\n\n","bodyDigest":"sha256:a36f8dc094113bfac4650dffa7c8f4dd4f661d66ba5738dcb62eac7002d47df7","bodyExcerpt":"Fixes #14150.","linkedIssues":["#14150"],"source":"explicit","title":"Only offer Remove > Theme when there is a theme to remove"},"createdAt":"2026-10-03T16:09:10Z","decisionSummary":{"claimEvidence":[{"claim":"requirement_preserved","claimId":"requirement:SW-REQ-260922-2JZT","failed":0,"notRun":0,"obligations":[{"class":"error_handling","failed":0,"passed":0,"skipped":0,"source":"inherited:SYS-REQ-260922-47T8","status":"not_linked","tests":0},{"class":"external_call_timeout_bounded","failed":0,"passed":0,"skipped":0,"source":"inherited:SYS-REQ-260922-47T8","status":"not_linked","tests":0}],"passed":2,"requirementId":"SW-REQ-260922-2JZT","status":"observed_pass","unknown":0},{"claim":"requirement_preserved","claimId":"requirement:SW-REQ-260922-3T3F","failed":0,"notRun":0,"obligations":[{"class":"boundary","failed":0,"passed":2,"skipped":0,"source":"own","status":"observed_pass","tests":2},{"class":"error_handling","failed":0,"passed":2,"skipped":0,"source":"own","status":"observed_pass","tests":2},{"class":"input_domain","failed":0,"passed":1,"skipped":0,"source":"own","status":"observed_pass","tests":1}],"passed":3,"requirementId":"SW-REQ-260922-3T3F","status":"observed_pass","unknown":0},{"claim":"requirement_preserved","claimId":"requirement:SW-REQ-260922-46HY","failed":0,"notRun":0,"obligations":[{"class":"boundary","failed":0,"observedVia":"SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW","passed":1,"skipped":0,"source":"inherited:SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW","status":"observed_pass","tests":1},{"class":"error_handling","failed":0,"observedVia":"SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW","passed":1,"skipped":0,"source":"inherited:SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW","status":"observed_pass","tests":1}],"passed":3,"requirementId":"SW-REQ-260922-4